> >>>> The 4.0.x release tests 4.0.x clients against 3.9.x brokers and the
> >>>> 3.9.x release tests 1.0.x clients against 3.9.x brokers. It is not cle=
ar
> >>>> to me why we need a bridge release in this case.
> >>>>
> >>>
> >>> We don't test client upgrades from 1.0.x to 4.0.x. They may work, but i=
t's
> >>> untested. Again, we are focusing on simplicity versus flexibility for e=
dge
> >>> cases. The number of people upgrading from 1.0 to 4.0 is very low (if n=
ot
> >>> zero).
> >>>
> >>> That's why I still think the simple description I provided in my other
> >>> message is the way to go
> >>>
> >>> Deprecated APIs may or may not affect users, so that has to be evaluate=
d on
> >>> a case by case basis.
> >>>
> >>> Ismael
