>
> Hi David,
>
> we found an issue with Kafka Streams that definitely is a regression. A
> commit fixed a leak, introduced a bug that prevented Kafka Streams from
> re-initializing its transactional producer in case the producer is
> fenced. The consequence of not re-initializing the transactional
> producer is an infinite loop of ProducerFencedExceptions with
> corresponding rebalances (approx every min).
>
> I opened a PR that reverts the defective commit:
> https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/19078
>
> We tested the revert in our internal soak and everything seems fine again=
.
>
> May I cherry-pick the revert to 4.0?
>
> Best,
> Bruno
