Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-18930) KRaft MigrationEvent won't retry
 when failing to write data to ZK
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Luke Chen created KAFKA-18930:
---------------------------------

             Summary: KRaft MigrationEvent won't retry when failing to writ=
e data to ZK=20
                 Key: KAFKA-18930
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18930
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
    Affects Versions: 3.9.0
            Reporter: Luke Chen


When running ZK migrating to KRaft, there will be a dual-write mode. In tha=
t mode, metadata will write to KRaft, then write to ZK asynchronously. When=
 there's some exception, KRaft MigrationEvent won't retry when failing to w=
rite data to ZK. That causes metadata inconsistency between KRaft and ZK.

=C2=A0

Besides, when doing KRaft controller clean shutdown, we should keep retryin=
g the failing ZK writing until force shutdown, to make sure the metadata is=
 consistent.

=C2=A0

The impact is when rolling back to ZK mode during migration, the metadata i=
n ZK is out of date



