Hi Luke,

+1 for backporting https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/19172.

Regarding the system tests, here is my take:
* kafkatest.tests.connect.connect_distributed_test - These tests are flaky
in our test infrastructure but they pass locally.
* kafkatest.tests.core.network_degrade_test - This is not a blocker as it
does not test any Kafka bits besides Trogdor.
* kafkatest.tests.tools.replica_verification_test - It has been failing for
a while. The tool is deprecated and not really used so I don't consider it
as a blocker. However, there is already a PR inflight to improve it.

Overall, system tests look pretty good to me. Do you agree?

Best,
David

