Hi David,

Thanks for the analysis.

> * kafkatest.tests.connect.connect_distributed_test - These tests are flak=
y
in our test infrastructure but they pass locally.

If they can be passed locally, it should be fine.

> * kafkatest.tests.core.network_degrade_test - This is not a blocker as it
does not test any Kafka bits besides Trogdor.

Hmm... from the test description, it is indeed not related to kafka itself.
But since we did huge change in this release, I'd like to be more careful.
I'll try to run this test suite in our internal environment again and
report the results here.

> * kafkatest.tests.tools.replica_verification_test - It has been failing
for
a while. The tool is deprecated and not really used so I don't consider it
as a blocker. However, there is already a PR inflight to improve it.

Sounds good to me.


Thanks.
Luke

