Jun Rao created KAFKA-18991:
-------------------------------

             Summary: AbstractFetcherThread should verify the current leade=
r epoch in the fetch request matches the leader epoch in the fetch state
                 Key: KAFKA-18991
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18991
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: core
            Reporter: Jun Rao


This is to follow up on [https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/18852#discuss=
ion_r1987826859.]

It's possible that a fetch response (for an old leader epoch) returns diver=
gingEndOffsets. In this case, we will take the divergingEndOffsets in the f=
etch response and truncates the local log based on that. This could cause a=
 committed record to be removed from the follow's log, potentially leading =
to data loss.

We can fix this issue by ignoring the fetch response if the leader epoch in=
 the fetch request doesn't match the leader epoch in the current fetch stat=
e.

=C2=A0



