Sean Quah created KAFKA-19023:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Snapshottable timers in the coordinator runtime
                 Key: KAFKA-19023
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19023
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: group-coordinator
            Reporter: Sean Quah
            Assignee: Sean Quah


In a couple of places, the coordinator runtime and group coordinator create and destroy timers, eg. for session timeouts.

When coordinator state is rolled back, these timer operations are not reverted. It would be nice to have these timers participate in the snapshot mechanism.



