Thanks TengYao,

I note that the KIP's scope has shrunk a bit, and the goal now is only to
upgrade slf4j to make it easy for users to replace log4j2 with another
slf4j binding, but Kafka will only ship with log4j2 and not alternatives,
so people who want to use something else will have to bring their own jars.

+1 (non-binding, not a committer) for that plan

