> To me, the main thing is really, that currently user can call `new` what m=
akes it easy to do thing wrong. If we change it to an interface, users canno=
t call `new`, and if the interface says "do not implement me", it should hop=
efully trigger the right response.

It seems we want to obstruct users from creating the object - that means we n=
eed to disable users to new/extend it. If I understand it correctly, using t=
he interface is a suitable way. Maybe we can have introduce a new annotation=
 to explicitly remind users not to implement the interface. If we are in Jav=
a 17, the annotation can be replaced by sealed keyword.

Best,
Chia-Ping



